Article 9

Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after children as they should be, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household sphere, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

3.6.text:
Article 25

1. In addition to forming Networked P2TP2A, the Regional Government shall form a Forum for Handling Victims of Violence against Women and Children (FPK2PA).
2. FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of district FPK2PA and sub-district FPK2PA.
3. The Organizational Structure of FPK2PA consists of:a. Patron;
b. Advisor;
c. Steering;
d. Chairperson;
e. Vice Chairperson;
f. Secretary;
g. Field Coordinator;
h. Members; andi. Secretariat Staff.
4. The establishment of District FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree. (5) The establishment of Sub-district FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Sub-district Head's Decree. (6) The Duties and Functions of FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (2) are:a. coordinating and synchronizing the handling of PPT services;
b. maintaining and developing networks and referral systems; andc. collecting, compiling, and presenting reports on violence.
7. FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (2) may receive and send case referrals from or to other service units in a networked manner.
8. Members of FPK2PA as referred to in paragraph (3) letter h consist of Regional Work Units that have duties and functions in the fields of social affairs, handling of women and children, health, education, youth and sports, religion, population, manpower, and/or industry and trade, as well as Vertical Agencies and community institutions grouped in the following fields:a. health field;
b. psychology field;
c. law field;
d. social field; ande. economic field.

Article 13

1. The organizational structure of the Networked P2TP2A as referred to in Article 12 paragraph (2) consists of:
a. General Chairperson;
b. Executive Chairperson who oversees the divisions;
c. Secretary; and
d. Treasurer.
2. The divisions as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d, at a minimum include:
a. complaints service division;
b. health service division;
c. social rehabilitation service division;
d. repatriation and social reintegration division; and
e. legal aid service division.

Article 19

The health service division as referred to in Article 13 paragraph (2) letter b has the duties of:
a. conducting examination, treatment, and follow-up care for victims;
b. conducting coordination of health rehabilitation implementation and medico-legal;
c. conducting medico-legal examination including collection of evidence from victims and preparation of visum et repertum;
d. conducting supporting examinations and laboratory tests on evidence;
e. conducting consultation with expert doctors or making referrals; and
f. preparing case reports.

Article 29

In the implementation of integrated services, every victim receives the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as a human being;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of identity;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/ori. the right to assistance.

Article 18

The complaints service division as referred to in Article 13 paragraph (2) letter a has the duties of:
a. conducting interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. making recommendations for follow-up services;
c. conducting coordination and referrals to follow-up services and related parties; and
d. conducting administration of the complaint process.

CHAPTER VIII

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 35

1. Every person participates in providing protection to women and child victims of violence. (2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:a. forming women and child protection institutions in villages whose duties are to carry out prevention, services, and supervision;
b. conducting socialization of women's and children's rights; c. providing assistance to victims;
d. reporting and referring to authorized agencies/institutions in the Sub-district if violence against victims occurs in their environment; ande. Authorized agencies/institutions in the Sub-district, if necessary, may refer to other agencies/institutions.

Article 9

Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after children as they should be, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household sphere, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

Article 28

Principles of service delivery to victims: a. fast;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not charged; andg. guaranteed confidentiality.

REGENT OF GUNUNGKIDUL,

Considering:
a. that all forms of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
b. that in addition to protection efforts, prevention, services, and empowerment are needed for women and children victims of violence;
c. that there is a need for regulation of efforts as referred to in letter b in the region;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
