CHAPTER VIII

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 35

1. Every person participates in providing protection to women and child victims of violence. (2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:a. forming women and child protection institutions in villages whose duties are to carry out prevention, services, and supervision;
b. conducting socialization of women's and children's rights; c. providing assistance to victims;
d. reporting and referring to authorized agencies/institutions in the Sub-district if violence against victims occurs in their environment; ande. Authorized agencies/institutions in the Sub-district, if necessary, may refer to other agencies/institutions.

Article 15

The executive chairperson as referred to in Article 13 paragraph (1) letter b has the duties of:
a. coordinating the duties and functions of each service division;
b. controlling the implementation of protection and handling programs for victims of violence;
c. conducting coordination and cooperation with related external parties;
d. collecting and utilizing resources effectively and efficiently for protection and handling activities for victims of violence; and
e. providing periodic reports to the Regent, specifically for victims of trafficking in persons, copies of reports are also given to the task force for prevention and handling of trafficking in persons.

Article 16

The Secretary as referred to in Article 13 paragraph (1) letter c has the duties of:
a. assisting the implementation of the duties of the General Chairperson;
b. assisting in preparing coordination activities and follow-up on protection, handling of victims of violence;
c. assisting in preparing work program plans for the central task force;
d. providing administrative services in the cooperation of the Central Task Force with Ministries/Agencies and Community Institutions that are members of the Central Task Force;
e. organizing service activities for the collection, processing, and presentation of data as well as preparation of secretariat activity reports; and
f. fostering and implementing working cooperation with Ministries/Agencies and related Community Institutions in the implementation of prevention and handling of trafficking in persons.

